Out of Memory Error: could not allocate block of size 256.0 KiB (15.2 MiB/15.2 MiB used)
Database is launched in in-memory mode and no temporary directory is specified.
Unused blocks cannot be offloaded to disk.

Launch the database with a persistent storage back-end
Or set SET temp_directory='/path/to/tmp.tmp'

Possible solutions:
* Reducing the number of threads (SET threads=X)
* Disabling insertion-order preservation (SET preserve_insertion_order=false)
* Increasing the memory limit (SET memory_limit='...GB')

See also https://duckdb.org/docs/current/guides/performance/how_to_tune_workloads
hint: -agent renders errors as JSON and results compactly for AI coding agents (duckdb -help lists all options)
